<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/15th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Sanluri</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1409">1409</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Sanluri was fought in June 1409 in southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sardinia">Sardinia</a>, where an Aragonese army led by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/martin-i-of-sicily">Martin the Younger</a>, King of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sicily">Sicily</a>, defeated the forces of the Judicate of Arborea under William of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/narbonne">Narbonne</a>. The defeat broke Arborea's resistance, and within a decade the last Sardinian judicate was absorbed by the Crown of Aragon.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-sanluri.jpg" alt="Battle of Sanluri" width="320" height="212" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Giovanni Marghinotti (1798-1865) · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:MarghinottibattagliaSanluri.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>The decisive <b>Battle of Sanluri</b> in 1409, won by Martin the Younger, King of Sicily, broke Arborean power, and the remaining rights were bought from William III of Narbonne in 1420.</blockquote><a href="/empire/kingdom-of-sardinia">Kingdom of Sardinia · Military</a></li><li><blockquote>Arborea's army was defeated by the Aragonese at <b>Sanluri</b> in 1409.</blockquote><a href="/state/judicate-of-arborea">Judicate of Arborea</a></li></ul></section>
